# docs_everywhere (Python)

Python bindings for the `docs_everywhere` native library, built on `ctypes`.

## Requirements

- Python 3.9 or later
- The native library (`libdocs_everywhere.so`, `libdocs_everywhere.dylib`, or `docs_everywhere.dll`)

## Install

```bash
pip install .
```

## Loading the native library

The bindings load the library from `DOCS_EVERYWHERE_LIBRARY` when it is set (a full path),
then from inside the installed package, then from the system loader's search
path.

## Usage

```python
import docs_everywhere
```

